<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Gonzaga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1328">1328</a>–<a href="/years/1708">1708</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Gonzaga dynasty, Gonzaga family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Gonzaga was an Italian princely family that ruled Mantua from 1328 to 1708, first as captains, then as marquesses from 1433 and dukes from 1530. Its branches also held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a>, Guastalla, Novellara and, through Louis Gonzaga's marriage to Henriette of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a> in 1565, the French duchy of Nevers. The family were major patrons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> artists such as Mantegna and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giulio-romano">Giulio Romano</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga.jpg" alt="House of Gonzaga" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MostEpic · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Gianfrancesco_I_Gonzaga,_Marquess_of_Mantua.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>House of Gonzaga</b> seized power in Mantua, in Lombardy, beginning a rule that lasted until 1708.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-16">16 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Gonzaga</b> overthrew the Bonacolsi in 1328, founding what became the Duchy of Mantua.</blockquote><a href="/state/commune-of-mantua">Commune of Mantua</a></li><li><blockquote>Its position between larger neighbours made it a pawn: the Este held it from 1289 to 1306, and in the 14th century it passed among various lords, including the <b>Gonzaga</b> under Feltrino Gonzaga and then the Visconti.</blockquote><a href="/state/commune-of-reggio">Commune of Reggio</a></li><li><blockquote>The Duchy of Nevers later went to the <b>Gonzagas</b> and the Mazarins, and lost its last rights in the Revolution.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-nevers">County of Nevers</a></li><li><blockquote>The state survived by careful loyalty to the emperors and good relations with the Este and <b>Gonzaga</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-novellara">County of Novellara</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1539 Countess Ludovica Torelli sold Guastalla to Ferrante Gonzaga, general of Charles V and governor of Milan, whose branch of the <b>Gonzaga</b> ruled it from then on.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-guastalla">Duchy of Guastalla</a></li></ul></section>
